@startuml Sequence_ReservationLifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2C6FAC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam noteBorderColor #E6800A
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5E6

title UseCase: Reservation Lifecycle — Confirm, Decline, Cancel & Auto-Complete

actor       "Admin"                    as Admin
actor       "User (Teacher/Student)"   as User
participant "ReservationController"    as Ctrl
participant "ReservationService"       as Svc
participant "ReservationRepository"    as ResRepo
participant "CompletionScheduler\n@cron 0 0/30 * * * *" as Scheduler

== Admin confirms a PENDING reservation (POST /api/reservations/{id}/confirm) ==

Admin -> Ctrl: POST /api/reservations/{id}/confirm\nAuthorization: Bearer <adminToken>\n{note: "Approved — enjoy the room!"}

activate Ctrl
note over Ctrl: @PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('RESERVATION_MANAGE')")

Ctrl -> Svc: confirm(id, adminId, req)
activate Svc

Svc -> ResRepo: findById(id)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{status: PENDING}

note over Svc: status == PENDING ✓

Svc -> Svc: reservation.status = CONFIRMED\nreservation.reviewedBy = adminId\nreservation.reviewNote = "Approved…"

Svc -> ResRepo: save(reservation)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{status: CONFIRMED}

Svc --> Ctrl: ReservationResponse{status: CONFIRMED}
deactivate Svc

Ctrl --> Admin: 200 OK\n{id, status:"CONFIRMED", reviewedBy:adminId, reviewNote:"Approved…"}
deactivate Ctrl

== Admin declines a PENDING reservation (POST /api/reservations/{id}/decline) ==

Admin -> Ctrl: POST /api/reservations/{id}/decline\nAuthorization: Bearer <adminToken>\n{note: "Room not available — maintenance"}

activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc: decline(id, adminId, req)
activate Svc

Svc -> ResRepo: findById(id)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{status: PENDING}

Svc -> Svc: reservation.status = DECLINED\nreservation.reviewedBy = adminId\nreservation.reviewNote = "Room not available…"

Svc -> ResRepo: save(reservation)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{status: DECLINED}

Svc --> Ctrl: ReservationResponse{status: DECLINED}
deactivate Svc

Ctrl --> Admin: 200 OK\n{status:"DECLINED", …}
deactivate Ctrl

== User cancels own CONFIRMED reservation (DELETE /api/reservations/{id}) ==
note over User: Reservation starts in the future

User -> Ctrl: DELETE /api/reservations/{id}\nAuthorization: Bearer <userToken>

activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc: cancel(id, auth)
activate Svc

Svc -> ResRepo: findById(id)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{userId=X, status:CONFIRMED, startDateTime: future}

note over Svc: callerId == reservation.userId ✓\nstatus ∈ [PENDING, CONFIRMED] ✓\nstartDateTime > now ✓

Svc -> Svc: reservation.status = CANCELLED

Svc -> ResRepo: save(reservation)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{status: CANCELLED}

Svc --> Ctrl: ReservationResponse{status: CANCELLED}
deactivate Svc

Ctrl --> User: 200 OK\n{status:"CANCELLED", …}
deactivate Ctrl

== Attempt to cancel already-started reservation (error flow) ==

User -> Ctrl: DELETE /api/reservations/{id}\n(startDateTime is in the past)
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc: cancel(id, auth)
activate Svc
Svc -> ResRepo: findById(id)
ResRepo --> Svc: Reservation{startDateTime: past}
note over Svc: startDateTime.isBefore(now) → ERROR
Svc --> Ctrl: throw BadRequestException\n("Cannot cancel a reservation that has already started")
deactivate Svc
Ctrl --> User: 400 Bad Request\n{"error":"Cannot cancel a reservation that has already started"}
deactivate Ctrl

== Scheduled auto-completion (every 30 minutes) ==

note over Scheduler: Spring @Scheduled\ncron: "0 0/30 * * * *"

Scheduler -> ResRepo: findConfirmedPastEnd(now)\n(status=CONFIRMED AND end_date_time < now)
ResRepo --> Scheduler: [Reservation1{id,…}, Reservation2{id,…}]

loop for each expired reservation
    Scheduler -> Scheduler: reservation.status = COMPLETED
end

Scheduler -> ResRepo: saveAll(expiredReservations)
ResRepo --> Scheduler: ok

note over Scheduler: Logs: "Completed 2 reservation(s) past their end time"

@enduml
